From: AltarsCN <337293323+Altars3668@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 19 Sep 2026 17:07:59 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] msxml3: take MSXML's \uXXXX escapes in a pattern facet.
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

XML Schema regular expressions have no numeric escape. The grammar allows \n,
\r, \t, the punctuation escapes, the character-class shorthands and \p{...}, and
nothing else. MSXML takes \uXXXX anyway, and schemas written against it use it
freely. libxml2 goes by the specification, refuses the facet, and with it the
whole schema -- one unusable pattern and IXMLDOMSchemaCollection::add fails
outright.

Office's App-V runtime keeps its deployment-configuration schema as an embedded
resource and adds it to a schema cache before it will configure a package. Two
of its facets are

  [^ï·-ï·¯￹-ï¿¿\p{IsPrivateUse}]+
  [^"&<>\u0000- \u007F\u0080-\u009F ­...]+

so under Wine that add failed with

  err:msxml:Schema_parse error code 1756: Element '{...XMLSchema}pattern':
    The value '...' of the facet 'pattern' is not a valid regular expression.
  fixme:msxml:cache_entry_from_xsd_doc failed to parse doc

and the Click-to-Run install ended at

  OISVAPI::ConfigurePackage Failed. publishScope = 1:
    [AppV Error: Code(0x3e504e25-0x80004005) ... File(xmlutils.cpp : 624)]
  error 30175

The escapes are rewritten to the characters they denote on the copy of the
document that goes to the schema parser, so nothing else sees them. U+0000
becomes U+0001: it cannot be held in a C string, and the two are
indistinguishable to a pattern matching XML content, which can contain neither.

Measured on the same install, resumed with only this changed:

  VirtualizationMechanism   AppVReady -> AppVRegistered
  HKLM Office keys          23 -> 2902
  setup.exe                 exit 106 -> exit 5

AppVRegistered is what the prefix imported from a real Windows machine reads.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
(cherry picked from commit ff1fb59cf2989dafc333e27f3feb795fe83a0c95)

diff --git a/dlls/msxml3/schema.c b/dlls/msxml3/schema.c
index 1427f213f3b..e6242a8b550 100644
--- a/dlls/msxml3/schema.c
+++ b/dlls/msxml3/schema.c
@@ -748,12 +748,86 @@ static BOOL link_datatypes(xmlDocPtr schema)
     return TRUE;
 }
 
+/* Turn MSXML's \uXXXX escapes in a pattern facet into the characters they mean.
+ *
+ * XML Schema regular expressions have no numeric escape at all -- the grammar
+ * allows \n, \r, \t, the punctuation escapes, the character-class shorthands
+ * and \p{...}, and nothing else.  MSXML takes \uXXXX anyway, and schemas
+ * written against it use it freely.  libxml2 goes by the specification, refuses
+ * the facet, and with it the whole schema: one unusable pattern and
+ * IXMLDOMSchemaCollection::add fails outright.
+ *
+ * Measured: Office's App-V runtime keeps its deployment-configuration schema as
+ * an embedded resource and adds it to a schema cache before it will configure a
+ * package.  Two of its facets are
+ *
+ *   [^\uFDD0-\uFDEF\uFFF9-\uFFFF\p{IsPrivateUse}]+
+ *   [^"&<>\u0000-\u0020\u007F\u0080-\u009F...]+
+ *
+ * so the schema never loaded, ConfigurePackage answered E_FAIL from its own
+ * xmlutils, and the Click-to-Run install failed the App-V step with 30175.
+ *
+ * U+0000 becomes U+0001: it cannot be held in a C string, and the two are
+ * indistinguishable to a pattern matching XML content, which can contain
+ * neither.
+ */
+static void rewrite_unicode_escapes(xmlNodePtr node)
+{
+    for (; node; node = node->next)
+    {
+        if (node->type != XML_ELEMENT_NODE) continue;
+
+        if (!xmlStrcmp(node->name, BAD_CAST "pattern"))
+        {
+            xmlChar *value = xmlGetProp(node, BAD_CAST "value");
+
+            if (value)
+            {
+                int len = xmlStrlen(value);
+                xmlChar *out = xmlMalloc(len + 1), *w = out;
+                const xmlChar *r = value;
+                BOOL changed = FALSE;
+
+                if (out)
+                {
+                    while (*r)
+                    {
+                        unsigned int cp;
+
+                        if (r[0] == '\\' && r[1] == 'u' &&
+                            sscanf((const char *)r + 2, "%4x", &cp) == 1 &&
+                            isxdigit(r[2]) && isxdigit(r[3]) && isxdigit(r[4]) && isxdigit(r[5]))
+                        {
+                            if (!cp) cp = 1;
+                            w += xmlCopyCharMultiByte(w, cp);
+                            r += 6;
+                            changed = TRUE;
+                        }
+                        else *w++ = *r++;
+                    }
+                    *w = 0;
+                    if (changed)
+                    {
+                        TRACE("rewrote pattern %s as %s\n", debugstr_a((char *)value),
+                              debugstr_a((char *)out));
+                        xmlSetProp(node, BAD_CAST "value", out);
+                    }
+                    xmlFree(out);
+                }
+                xmlFree(value);
+            }
+        }
+        rewrite_unicode_escapes(node->children);
+    }
+}
+
 static cache_entry* cache_entry_from_xsd_doc(xmlDocPtr doc, xmlChar const* nsURI, MSXML_VERSION v)
 {
     cache_entry* entry = malloc(sizeof(cache_entry));
     xmlSchemaParserCtxtPtr spctx;
     xmlDocPtr new_doc = xmlCopyDoc(doc, 1);
 
+    rewrite_unicode_escapes((xmlNodePtr)new_doc->children);
     link_datatypes(new_doc);
 
     /* TODO: if the nsURI is different from the default xmlns or targetNamespace,
